  static _null = 0 U'\000', static _replacement_char = 65533 U'�'}
(gdb) print class_list.getptr(inherits)
$4 = (const DocData::ClassDoc *) 0x0
(gdb) print class_list.getptr(symbol_class_name)
$5 = (const DocData::ClassDoc *) 0x29d64278
```

So surprisingly it's not `Test99` (the new `class_name` I used in my test to trigger the bug) which isn't found in available classes, but the `MyTool` it inherits, which I didn't modify. So somehow modifying the inheriting named class invalidates the class it inherits.

We can easily workaround the crash by just not dereferencing a nullptr, but the above might warrant further investigation as it sounds weird. For now I'll PR the workaround to fix the crash.
